 "about": "A coin that cannot be sold (every sell fails on chain: a honeypot, a curve that is finished, no route). A copy with one timed sell: everything at +2 s. Real trades. The +2 s sell is out, with the whole bag reserved, when the user presses Sell now: the button answers ok having sold nothing (documented: the step has the coins out) and the exit is written down as owed. The step fails; the rest of Sell now is tried and fails; from then on the settling pass tries it again every 30 s, and every try writes the same line into the feed: \"Sell of X (you pressed Sell now) failed: ...\". 21 identical lines in 10 minutes here, 2,880 a day, while the step's own endless retry writes two lines in all (the engine's rule: one feed line per failing sell, not one per retry). The feed keeps the newest 5,000 lines per user: in under two days nothing else is left in it.",
